    "selection_rule": "Per routing/N group, decompose each cell's per-launch event median as waves*(fixed_span + k_tiles*round) + empty_waves*slot over the non-production K sweep by least squares, with waves=ceil(active_ctas/104) and the empty-wave slot fixed at 405 ns from the independent bm32_round_cadence early-exit grid scan. fixed_span_ns is the sparse_n1600 group fill (the 7-point K sweep at production-like 40% active density); the other three groups are stability evidence only. The per-round service is analytic in the Forward model (DRAM bytes per round-wave at the hardware DRAM capacity plus the pipeline-depth-amortized DRAM latency); the measured group slopes 1098-1143 ns versus the analytic 1075-1141 ns validate that expression and select no measured round coefficient. local_k_round_interval_ns is the register-only BF16 MMA round service derived from the canonical BM32 MMA occupancy reference (2*32*64*128 flops at 1352.660353 flops/AP-cycle, 1.8 GHz). empty_wave_slot_ns is the bm32_round_cadence_r1 early-exit grid-scan slope; the all-empty source-exact prefix launches (3035 ns/wave) measure only the pure front-end launch-rate ceiling and are rejected for mixed launches because the four routing groups' fills become mutually inconsistent under it."
  },
